# Run outputs: checkpoints and datasets are far too large to track (runs/ is ~6.8G).
# The exceptions are the small provenance files the campaign log cites as evidence —
# per-epoch metrics and dataset generation_config — which are a few KB each and are
# useless to reconstruct after the fact. `!runs/**/` lets git descend to reach them.
runs/**
!runs/**/
!runs/**/metrics.jsonl
!runs/**/meta.json
# Phase 2 (chunk 9): iterations.jsonl is a campaign's only durable narrative —
# ~50 rows for a 24h run and nothing else survives the process — and
# provenance.json is the git SHA and config fingerprint that make those rows
# interpretable. Same argument as metrics.jsonl, same few KB.
!runs/**/iterations.jsonl
!runs/**/provenance.json
!runs/ANCHORS.sha256
# Chunk 10 + the M3 close-out (2026-08-11): the ladder log is the *verdict*, and
# it was ignored — RUNLOG-p2_a.md cites every one of these files as its evidence
# and none of them would have entered the repo. Same argument as iterations.jsonl
# and the same failure mode as the four incidents in test_gitignore_musttrack.py:
# a record the project depends on, silently unversioned. 104 KB for all of p2_a's.
# config.yaml is here because a run's *resolved* config is what makes its rows
# reproducible; the campaign reads this copy, not configs/.
!runs/**/ladder.jsonl
!runs/**/ladder_diagnostic.jsonl
!runs/**/ladder_diagnostic_r*.jsonl
!runs/**/config.yaml
!runs/**/triage_mate2_*.json
!runs/**/diagnose_mate2_*.txt
!runs/**/diag_value_*.json
!runs/**/s4_flip_*.json
# Perturbations carry their cause. annotations.jsonl explains blips in a run's
# own timing series -- a GPU-contention window, a manual intervention -- keyed by
# iteration, so iterations.jsonl can be read six weeks out without the reader
# having to reconstruct why one row is slow. Same family as calibration_note and
# the ladder's role field: the record answers its own obvious question.
!runs/**/annotations.jsonl
!runs/**/watchlist_coverage_*.json
!runs/**/semantic_residual_*.json
!runs/**/competitor_q_trajectory.json
!runs/**/track1_ckpt_iter*.json
!runs/**/p2_verdict_reps.json
# One directory holding several checkpoints' reps needs one verdict per checkpoint
# (PREREG-p2_e Addendum 3, runs/p2_d_midrun/).
!runs/**/p2_verdict_reps_*.json
# The arm-against-arm verdict of an A/B round (PREREG-p2_i K1, runs/p2_i_row/).
!runs/**/p2i_verdict_*.json
# PREREG-p2_j's K3 (`eval_reps.py m4`) and L2 (`ring_book_rows.py --json`) records.
!runs/**/p2_m4_*.json
!runs/**/book_rows.json
# PREREG-p2_g Step 0b: the training-step numbers from each stack.
!runs/**/bridge_*.json
!runs/**/reps_iter*.jsonl
!runs/**/ladder_pairscores.jsonl
# The mate-in-2 *tuning* suite (BLOCKED-2026-08-08 stage 2): the disjoint set the
# eval-profile sweep was selected on, cited by 18 results.jsonl rows and by the
# sweep firewall, and the one file that lets anyone re-check the disjointness
# claim. 36 KB. Its meta.json was tracked; the suite itself was not
# (REVIEW-2026-10-21 E10).
!runs/data/*/mate_in_*.epd

# Root-scoped: a bare `data/` would also swallow runs/data/ as a directory ignore,
# and git cannot descend into an ignored directory to reach the negations above.
/data/
__pycache__/
*.pt
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.dat
*.npy
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
uv.lock
*.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Review bundles zipped for external review (regenerable)
*.zip

# Machine-local Claude Code settings (and the atomic-write temp files it leaves)
.claude/settings.local.json*
*.tmp.*
